The model can now delegate to a named agent file, and the project-trust gate shipped in the same commit. fmt, clippy -D warnings and the full test suite all pass, and the working tree is clean.

Commits
• `40028335` (the src/ change, from the interrupted run):
  • A new tool named agent, with subagent_type and prompt parameters, in a new file src/agent_dispatch.rs.
  • It is only offered when at least one agent file can actually run. Someone with no agent files, or only untrusted project ones, sees exactly the same tool list as before.
  • Agents from your home directory always run. Agents defined inside a project only run when yoyo is started with --trust-project. Otherwise they're left out of the tool's description, and calling one gets a refusal that names the file and the flag.
  • Trust is checked again on every call, so a /cd that revokes trust also blocks those agents.
  • The description lists only name: description, capped at 8,000 bytes and cut safely on multi-byte characters. A file's body never appears in it; it becomes the child agent's instructions only when that agent is called.
  • The child agent is built the same way sub_agent is, so it gets the same deny rules, directory limits, --read-only-subagents setting and model. agent was added to BUILTIN_TOOL_NAMES.
• `c58eaead` (this run): the commands docs page had said agent files were "not yet used", which is no longer true. It now explains how delegation works, the --trust-project requirement, and what isn't supported yet. There is a new ARCHITECTURE.md entry for src/agent_dispatch.rs, and the old "nothing reads body as a prompt yet" line is marked superseded rather than deleted.

Gate check: I disabled the project-trust check (marked NEUTERED) and ran the agent_dispatch tests in one command. Five tests failed by name, including project_scope_def_untrusted_is_refused_with_name_file_and_remedy and live_trust_revocation_refuses_a_project_agent_granted_at_build. I then restored the file with git checkout, and all 9 passed again. Those test names are recorded in c58eaead's commit body; 40028335 was committed before the check ran.

Not done yet:
• yoyo agents doesn't mark untrusted project agents as unable to run.
• The frontmatter model and maxTurns keys are ignored.
• There's no fallback-model retry, and an agent can't call another named agent.
• There's no REPL /agents command.
• Agent files in subfolders of an agents directory aren't read.

I posted both the in-progress and landed comments on #1250, with those follow-ups and the next steps: REPL /agents, then milestone 3 (model/maxTurns).
